diff --git a/docs/development.md b/docs/development.md
index b8c3e65..bda471c 100644
--- a/docs/development.md
+++ b/docs/development.md
@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@ bin/rails dev:email
 
 Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
+### Push notifications
+
+Push notifications can be turned on from the notification settings in development too. Without `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` in the environment, Fizzy generates a throwaway VAPID key pair the first time it boots and keeps it in `tmp/vapid_key.pem`, so the devices you turn on keep working across restarts.
+
 ## SaaS gem
 
 37signals bundles Fizzy with [`fizzy-saas`](https://github.com/basecamp/fizzy/tree/main/saas), a companion gem that links Fizzy with our billing system and contains our production setup.
diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..009bc26 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -101,6 +101,26 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send push notifications to your users' phones and desktops through their browsers, so whatever lands in their notifications tray also reaches their devices.
+Browsers' push services require the server to identify itself with a [VAPID](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8292) key pair.
+Generate one with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails web_push:vapid_key
+```
+
+Then set the pair in the `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` environment variables:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=... --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=... ...
+```
+
+Keep using the same pair once people have turned notifications on: a new pair means every device has to be turned on again.
+Push services are given a contact address for your instance too, derived from `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` by default; set `VAPID_SUBJECT` (a `mailto:` or `https:` URL) to override it.
+Without a key pair, push notifications simply aren't offered in the notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
