+### Configuring push notifications (optional)
+
+To let people turn on push notifications for their phones and desktops, add a VAPID key pair to `.kamal/secrets` and list both in `env/secret` in `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` & `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`: generate the pair with `bin/rails web_push:vapid_key`, and keep it stable once people have turned notifications on.
+
+Optionally, set `VAPID_SUBJECT` (a `mailto:` or `https:` URL) as the contact address given to the push services; it defaults to your `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`.
+
 ### Configuring file storage (Active Storage)
 
 Production uses the local disk service by default. To use any other service defined in `config/storage.yml`, set `ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE`.
diff --git a/lib/tasks/web_push.rake b/lib/tasks/web_push.rake
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2800881
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/tasks/web_push.rake
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+namespace :web_push do
+  desc "Generate a VAPID key pair for web push notifications"
+  task vapid_key: :environment do
+    key = WebPush.generate_key
+
+    puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}"
